{"title":"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Note\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Note</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> a positive integer, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/f/eef0203e65664bd00b5f0325c5c5fcd81bcead8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" /> be the quotient obtained when the sum of all positive divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/9/bd923e41635af40a1abe58f230732f2280b0723a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/0/a30498646d780aea6d03d5130640089c4775112f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(14)=(1+2+7+14)\\div 14=\\frac{12}{7}\\]\" width=\"278\" height=\"37\" />\nWhat is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/9/059ad8410129b7b6d6472694ce2e970886214e31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(768)-f(384)?$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"137\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/0/8509bd8d874aef5999179b8e0e3fdbb2e45f09ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{1}{768} \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{1}{192} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 1 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{4}{3} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{8}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"403\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The prime factorizations of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/c/7dcd87737949216c3dbdabe299c062da63660425.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$768$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/5/c5505e205bbb801f064d35b4597cf46ee13842a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$384$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/2/732df098b65a830d14bf0f696ecb4f9ec2351f1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^8\\cdot3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/7/e47eb3bf2b399ea9a46cd156a912ada53ad8a7d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^7\\cdot3,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"20\" /> respectively. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/f/eef0203e65664bd00b5f0325c5c5fcd81bcead8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" /> is the sum of all fractions of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/6/2568f3ec9816df72713f34bebb886fc344c66276.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac 1d,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is a positive divisor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/9/bd923e41635af40a1abe58f230732f2280b0723a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> By geometric series, it follows that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f42717299c9f40c9c5694dcca7214e4896bcfc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{alignat*}{8} f(768)&amp;=\\left(\\sum_{k=0}^{8}\\frac{1}{2^k}\\right)+\\left(\\sum_{k=0}^{8}\\frac{1}{2^k\\cdot3}\\right)&amp;&amp;=\\frac{511}{256}+\\frac{511}{768}&amp;&amp;=\\frac{2044}{768}, \\\\ f(384)&amp;=\\left(\\sum_{k=0}^{7}\\frac{1}{2^k}\\right)+\\left(\\sum_{k=0}^{7}\\frac{1}{2^k\\cdot3}\\right)&amp;&amp;=\\frac{255}{128}+\\frac{255}{384}&amp;&amp;=\\frac{1020}{384}. \\end{alignat*}\" width=\"454\" height=\"114\" />\nTherefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/a/6cacefcab2941e11df27e57defe563192dc7843c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(768)-f(384)=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{1}{192}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"234\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~lopkiloinm ~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The prime factorization of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/5/c5505e205bbb801f064d35b4597cf46ee13842a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$384$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/7/e47eb3bf2b399ea9a46cd156a912ada53ad8a7d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^7\\cdot3,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"20\" /> so each of its positive divisors is of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/9/f2949376cf9667bec6117d164f65945d8a2c049f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^m$\" width=\"20\" height=\"12\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/b/6fb853a835bfa3ed324f4044ae879a3045554c55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^m\\cdot3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> for some integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/d/eadde1dc34fa5f76992240ee977d43cbdbc1316b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\leq m\\leq7.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"90\" height=\"16\" /> We will use this fact to calculate the sum of all its positive divisors. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/4/0445057f5439e7b6d2a6efe011ec3bc488370d06.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2^m + 2^m\\cdot3 = 2^m\\cdot(1+3) = 2^m\\cdot4 = 2^m\\cdot2^2 = 2^{m+2}\\]\" width=\"406\" height=\"20\" /> is the sum of the two forms of positive divisors for all such <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/9/269981c02d6475e9e4ac1869e1b063ef377c2847.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m.$\" width=\"19\" height=\"8\" /> By geometric series, the sum of all positive divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/5/c5505e205bbb801f064d35b4597cf46ee13842a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$384$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/4/03424922411f42837eba4dbd4dff73ad5016ffcb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{k=2}^{9}2^k = \\frac{2^{10}-2^2}{2-1} = 1020,\\]\" width=\"200\" height=\"51\" /> from which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/1/52181bec71c547fe263ba081c181e05d14e11570.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(384) = \\frac{1020}{384}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"124\" height=\"38\" /> Similarly, since the prime factorization of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/c/7dcd87737949216c3dbdabe299c062da63660425.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$768$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/7/ec7c3574a3a68c20feb4a3c0d6197f6fcc2a590a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^8 \\cdot 3,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"20\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/0/56094e08232ed6f63854515c6f948c1be7ba0f55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(768) = \\frac{2044}{768}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"124\" height=\"38\" /> \n</p><p>Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/a/6cacefcab2941e11df27e57defe563192dc7843c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(768)-f(384)=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{1}{192}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"234\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~mahaler\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/b/4eb912f901cc0dba33ac9d06a90b262b423d9eb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sigma(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"18\" /> denotes the sum of all positive divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/4/c54e7152acd659788861f0453ac195c635e0a005.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/1/0011102b1483e08ba3b68143ec49a3dcc9d01ed8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)=\\sigma(n)\\div n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"136\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/1/131be178aa95a399cd4293220bd35420135ce6cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=\\prod_{i=1}^{k}p_i^{e_i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"84\" height=\"56\" /> is the prime factorization of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/9/bd923e41635af40a1abe58f230732f2280b0723a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/b/4eb912f901cc0dba33ac9d06a90b262b423d9eb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sigma(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"18\" /> is multiplicative, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5b2ac2f5014e1eb325e5934fa16298e4060774.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sigma(n)=\\sigma\\left(\\prod_{i=1}^{k}p_i^{e_i}\\right)=\\prod_{i=1}^{k}\\sigma\\left(p_i^{e_i}\\right)=\\prod_{i=1}^{k}\\left(\\sum_{j=0}^{e_i}p_i^j\\right)=\\prod_{i=1}^{k}\\frac{p_i^{e_i+1}-1}{p_i-1}\\]\" width=\"494\" height=\"54\" /> by geometric series.\n</p><p>The prime factorizations of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/c/7dcd87737949216c3dbdabe299c062da63660425.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$768$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/5/c5505e205bbb801f064d35b4597cf46ee13842a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$384$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/2/732df098b65a830d14bf0f696ecb4f9ec2351f1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^8\\cdot3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/7/e47eb3bf2b399ea9a46cd156a912ada53ad8a7d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^7\\cdot3,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"20\" /> respectively. Note that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/c/50caf26a3cadf723b201c9cfdc12f378ccaea7d5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{alignat*}{8} f(768) &amp;= \\left(\\frac{2^9-1}{2-1}\\cdot\\frac{3^2-1}{3-1}\\right)\\div768 &amp;&amp;= \\frac{2044}{768}, \\\\ f(384) &amp;= \\left(\\frac{2^8-1}{2-1}\\cdot\\frac{3^2-1}{3-1}\\right)\\div384 &amp;&amp;= \\frac{1020}{384}. \\end{alignat*}\" width=\"337\" height=\"93\" />\nTherefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/a/6cacefcab2941e11df27e57defe563192dc7843c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(768)-f(384)=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{1}{192}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"234\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/e/6def76f334a76988548f8751af389caf86005cd1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 384 &amp;= 2^7\\cdot3, \\\\ 768 &amp;= 2^8\\cdot3. \\end{align*}\" width=\"93\" height=\"43\" />\nBoth numbers take the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/6/3a61ffe913989d355cd897d91ab21c616760f114.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n\\cdot3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"14\" />. Define a function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/0965bf432b818b46740e3cd4d042899628c7ad0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> as being the sum of the factors for any number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/6/3a61ffe913989d355cd897d91ab21c616760f114.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n\\cdot3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"14\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is a nonnegative integer.\n</p><p>If you list out the factors of a number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/6/3a61ffe913989d355cd897d91ab21c616760f114.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n\\cdot3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"14\" />, all the factors are even except for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. So to produce a list of factors for the number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/b/47bd8a3d6dc9ccca631e3d36b9bc821b071954cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{n+1}\\cdot3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"17\" />, you can multiply all the factors on the first list by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and then add on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/8/a486f26f9821fb48001925bfbd035a26cf4b49a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(n) = 2S(n-1) + 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"172\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>We need to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/6/796c9311491f6c09125097afcfb446a7b35ac034.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{S(8)}{768} - \\frac{S(7)}{384}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"103\" height=\"40\" />. This can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/5/945dd86b8983ad95dc63c74a7e972fd02132505f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2S(7)+4-2S(7)}{768}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"148\" height=\"40\" />. Our recursive formula states that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/8/a486f26f9821fb48001925bfbd035a26cf4b49a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(n) = 2S(n-1) + 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"172\" height=\"20\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/5/a35b801c9c77f3c8dd5a51557b4f97d53942c6d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(n) - 2S(n-1) = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"172\" height=\"20\" />. Thus, the fraction simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/2/272b699f2eaf16cd602e35615ba7150a69c44b77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{768} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{1}{192}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"134\" height=\"49\" />. Note that we never needed to figure out what <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/2/0428e5f3f7e5e7b92b8108f0cd2c25a01702f90e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(8)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/c/77cc0ad8e9b11641701c8089a9c3280c2fce3740.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(7)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> were, sparing us a lot of calculation.\n</p><p>~Curious_crow\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We know that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/e/6fe74ab589e59f26c8a60dd8cdb4432a669566ce.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} f(768) &amp;= \\frac{1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + \\cdots + 768}{768}, \\\\ f(384) &amp;= \\frac{1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + \\cdots + 384}{384}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"280\" height=\"81\" />\nWe want to find the difference of these so\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/3/1f37deec06f197b84b07ded022e6332e300a044d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + \\cdots + 768}{768} - \\frac{ 2(1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + \\cdots + 384)}{2\\cdot384} = \\frac{1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + \\cdots + 768}{768} - \\frac{ 2 + 4 + 6 + 8 + \\cdots + 768}{768}.\\]\" width=\"877\" height=\"38\" />\nWe are only left with the even divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/c/7dcd87737949216c3dbdabe299c062da63660425.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$768$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> on the fraction on the right so the answer would be the sum of all odd divisors  of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/c/7dcd87737949216c3dbdabe299c062da63660425.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$768$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />) over <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/c/7dcd87737949216c3dbdabe299c062da63660425.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$768$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/9/ea973bb0a2cc50b162375b4eca93867ff611ad7d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1 + 3}{768}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{1}{192}}.\\]\" width=\"146\" height=\"48\" />\n~pengf\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As in Solution 1, the prime factorization of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/c/7dcd87737949216c3dbdabe299c062da63660425.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$768$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/b/ecbe453d71bf3313ed12846d6bb2fc7c25fe15f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^8 \\cdot 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"17\" />, and the prime factorization of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/5/c5505e205bbb801f064d35b4597cf46ee13842a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$384$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/3/8934e8dbe5b43a21f1e26fc4149b05d7ea63eb13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^7 \\cdot 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"17\" />. Recalling the sum of factors formula and sum of the powers of 2 formula, we find that the sum of the factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/c/7dcd87737949216c3dbdabe299c062da63660425.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$768$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/e/17e8bd7fa5c6a458446e2eee8cc899430c533d5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1+2^1+2^2+2^3+2^4+2^5+2^6+2^7+2^8)(1+3^1)=(2^9-1)(4)=(511)(4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"595\" height=\"21\" />, and the sum of factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/5/c5505e205bbb801f064d35b4597cf46ee13842a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$384$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/1/301b82c0eba4d42fbd7e54e956fff7293e7ffed3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+2^1+2^2+2^3+2^4+2^5+2^6+2^7)(1+3^1)=(2^8-1)(4)=(255)(4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"550\" height=\"21\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/8/ab80acf1124521bb2168611f859666d1885dbc77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(768)=\\frac{(511)(4)}{768}=\\frac{511}{192}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"202\" height=\"40\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/7/3e72bb996159ab55c654517c8d9c79a727f0d322.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(384)=\\frac{(255)(4)}{384}=\\frac{510}{192}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"202\" height=\"40\" />. So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/4/0e4a364dd134ba15f0002fc67c6ea92f93462b1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(768)-f(384)=\\frac{511}{192}-\\frac{510}{192}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{1}{192}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"338\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~ <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Cxsmi\">cxsmi</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Note\">Note</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Note\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Note that you can cut away some of the arithmetic by realizing that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/8/108a73ba9e2158bd20a39743526c28869c82eb2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2^8-1) \\cdot 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"86\" height=\"21\" /> is 1 less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/8/3a891d6c397a6fe781e9867b479ebb3663fdc725.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^9-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" />.\n~bird987\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7\">Solution 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Observe that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/f/eef0203e65664bd00b5f0325c5c5fcd81bcead8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" /> equals the sum of the reciprocals of the positive divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. Since 768 is a multiple of 384, every divisor of 384 will also be a divisor of 768. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/c/83c43b98f339aa5eac639af288d2543556a54630.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(768)-f(384)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"129\" height=\"20\" /> equals the sum of the reciprocals of the positive divisors of 768 which are not divisors of 384. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/0/9e054ec5b755912105c9b74ca34eea72d7ea5a03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$768 = 2^8 \\cdot 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"92\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/6/0661a388a75679edc931e83e699f8d53ec6af170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$384 = 2^7 \\cdot 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"92\" height=\"17\" />, the divisors of 768 which are not divisors of 384 are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/3/6b32901dd20471881cf91f3661abe41d60f12b5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^8 = 256$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"70\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/b/88b43cf3058667670fcb889d31ab9b08b5e4ca25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^8 \\cdot 3 = 768$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"92\" height=\"17\" />. Therefore\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/f/ddff7567d05fb6dbe320dda4779228813f084643.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(768)-f(384) = \\frac{1}{256} + \\frac{1}{768} = \\frac{3 + 1}{768} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B) } \\frac{1}{192}}.\\]\" width=\"409\" height=\"48\" />\n~scrabbler94\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/jgyyGeEKhwk?t=1116\">https://youtu.be/jgyyGeEKhwk?t=1116</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/FFlj8W_xkPc\">https://youtu.be/FFlj8W_xkPc</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B\">2021 Fall AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017200901\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.054 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.077 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 591/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2448/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 308/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 18239/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.244      1 -total\n 60.47%    8.009      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 37.87%    5.015      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:22256:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017200901 and revision id 285549. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}